974. Subarray Sums Divisible by K
Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return the number of non-empty subarrays that have a sum divisible by k.

Explanation:
The same logic as before for divisible by k;
So we are going to store the number of times the remainder appears in the hashmap as we are going to take the count
Key Idea — Same Remainder

If two prefix sums have the same remainder when divided by k, subtracting them cancels the remainders, so their difference (the subarray sum) is divisible by k.
Therefore, store remainder → frequency in the HashMap. If the current remainder has appeared x times, it forms x valid subarrays → count += x.


Code:
class Solution {
    public int subarraysDivByK(int[] nums, int k) {
        int count=0;
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int prefixSum=0; map.put(0,1);
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            prefixSum+=nums[i];
            int rem = prefixSum%k;
            if(rem<0){
                rem+=k;
            }
            if(map.containsKey(rem)){
                count+=map.get(rem);
            }

            map.put(rem,map.getOrDefault(rem,0)+1);
        }
        return count;
    }
}
